{
  "id": "challenge-road-1999",
  "name": "Challenge Road 1999",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "Challenge Road 1999 Summer was the run of regional tournaments that opened Japan's Grand Party 1999-2000 season: nine tournaments at seven venues, from Osaka on 10 July to Sapporo on 10 August 1999, during the school holidays. It had two divisions, the junior Tropical Mega Battle, up to the sixth year of elementary school, and the senior Secret Super Battle, up to the second year of high school.\n\nThe top three of each tournament won cosmos holo No. 1, No. 2 and No. 3 Trainer trophy cards. The Tropical Mega Battle's show Ken Sugimori's Exeggutor on the division's logo, and only its No. 1 card gave a place at the Best in Japan final, played in Hawaii in August 1999 alongside the first International Tropical Mega Battle. The Secret Super Battle's show Hideki Kazama's silhouette of Mewtwo beside a gold, silver or bronze Poké Ball, and all three gave a place at its final, held in Tokyo on 22 August 1999 at a venue kept secret. Every player in each Tropical Mega Battle final, 64 at each of the nine, got Tropical Wind, so 576 were handed out.",
